\\\",\n  \\\"requirement\\\":\\\"An entry that a leader acknowledges to a client must be stored by a majority of the configuration in force at the time, and must be present in the log of any leader later elected from that configuration.\\\",\n  \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"Raft itself: the leader's commit rule and quorum accounting use the configuration the node recovered, and the node's own recovery path is what leaves that configuration behind the log's committed history.\\\",\n  \\\"anchors\\\":[\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-commitment\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"recalculate\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":88,\\\"end_line\\\":88},\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-quorum\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"quorumSize\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1087,\\\"end_line\\\":1087},\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-scan\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"NewRaft\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":508,\\\"end_line\\\":508}\n  ],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"stale-restart\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"stale_config_restart\\\",\n    \\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"live_voters_after_restart\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},\n                  {\\\"field\\\":\\\"log_has_config_entry_beyond_snapshot\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":true},\n                  {\\\"field\\\":\\\"true_quorum\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3}]}\n  ],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"stale_config_write\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"variant\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"stale-restart\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"write_backed_by_true_quorum\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"The write the stale-configuration leader acknowledges is held by at least a majority of the five-voter configuration in force.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"stale_config_loss\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"variant\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"stale-restart\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"acknowledged_write_absent_from_new_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"The acknowledged write survives in the leader elected from the configuration in force.\\\"}\n  ]\n },\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[\n  {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"a867b593d52841198a36a897ae6a8f0a-question-1\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-scan\\\",\\\"s-restore-committed\\\",\\\"s-commitment\\\",\\\"s-quorum\\\",\\\"s-runfollower-gate\\\"],\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Current account (source-derived, measurement pending): a leader's commit rule is computed from r.configurations.latest, which commitment.setConfiguration and quorumSize consume; when a restart leaves that configuration behind the log's committed history, a node that then leads uses the smaller voter set for both its quorum and its replication set, so it can acknowledge a write that a majority of the configuration in force never stores, and a leader elected from that configuration can be elected without the entry. The mechanism on the source side is: restoreFromCommittedLogs applies logs up to the recovered commit index and the scan then starts after it, so the recommitted configuration entry is never loaded, while the entry that records the change remains in the log; quorumSize and commitment both count voters from the recovered configuration, and commitment.recalculate commits the (n-1)/2-th match index of that set. The discrimination is the queued experiment: it restarts the node under test from a snapshot that records a three-voter configuration while the configuration in force has five voters, transfers leadership to it, and checks whether the acknowledged write is backed by a true majority and whether it survives in a leader elected from the configuration in force. Local construction feedback of these harness bytes showed the chain end to end, including acknowledged apply error nil with only two holders out of five voters and a later leader without the payload; those local numbers are construction feedback only and are not retained evidence, so the conclusion stays conditional until the receipt is read.\\\",\n   \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"conditional\\\",\n   \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"unresolved\\\",\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n    \\\"The configuration gap needs a snapshot taken while a smaller configuration was committed, plus later entries that advance the recovered commit index past the recommitting entry; a cluster that snapshots after every configuration change may not reach that state.\\\",\n    \\\"A later configuration entry or an installed snapshot repairs the recovered configuration, and the experiment deliberately prevents repair by isolating one voter and by keeping the configuration stable.\\\",\n    \\\"The local construction run is not retained evidence; the phase ordering it exercises (transfer, disconnection, shutdown of holders) could behave differently under the controller's execution.\\\"\n   ],\n   \\\"limitations\\\":[\n    \\\"Applies to nodes with RestoreCommittedLogs=true and a LogStore implementing CommitTrackingLogStore.\\\",\n    \\\"Measured history is a single in-memory five-voter cluster with authored commands and the repository's in-memory stores; production stores, multi-datacenter latencies and concurrent client traffic are not covered.\\\",\n    \\\"The acknowledgement is observed through the Apply future of the node under test; the loss is observed as absence of the payload from the later leader's log store, which does not by itself prove that no other surviving node could later resurrect the entry.\\\"]}\n ]\n}\njson.dump(u,open('update.json','w'),indent=2); print('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 32, in <module>\nNameError: name 'true' is not defined. Did you mean: 'True'?\n{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"1bdd60fe5af14a33879d92997922e21b\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 1256.278107710008, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\", \"no_change\": true, \"execution_requested\": false, \"effects\": [{\"object\": \"investigations\", \"action\": \"unchanged\", \"targets\": [\"a867b593d52841198a36a897ae6a8f0a-question-1\"]}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
